---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Week 5 Day 1: Layered Architecture Reviewer Checklist & Audit | MFS Internship" currentPath="/manager-review">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs & Header -->
    <div style="padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a href="/manager-review" style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; text-decoration: none;">&larr; Manager Portal</a>
        <span style="color: var(--text-muted);">&bull;</span>
        <a href="/milestones" style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; text-decoration: none;">Milestones</a>
        <span style="color: var(--text-muted);">&bull;</span>
        <span class="badge badge-warning" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">Week 5 • Day 1 Review</span>
        <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">Nov 2–3, 2026</span>
      </div>

      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem;">
        <div>
          <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 700;">
            Week 5, Day 1: Layered Architecture &amp; Serverless Entry — Reviewer Hub
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-subtitle" style="margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 860px;">
            Master reviewer checklist, codebase ground-truth verification (<code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> &amp; <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code>), and side-by-side evaluation of submissions from <strong>Mg Phyo Min Htet</strong> and <strong>Ma Yamin Aye</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;" class="no-print">
          <a href="#chat-feedback-box" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">
            <span>Copy Chat Feedback &darr;</span>
          </a>
          <button onclick="window.print()" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">
            <span>Print Review PDF</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Jump Bar -->
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.25rem;" class="no-print">
        <a href="#assignment-brief" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Assignment Task</a>
        <a href="#reviewer-checklist" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Interactive Reviewer Checklist</a>
        <a href="#comparison-matrix" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Side-by-Side Scorecard</a>
        <a href="#intern-reviews" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Detailed Audit (Phyo vs. Yamin)</a>
        <a href="#dependency-chains" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Dependency Chain Diagrams</a>
        <a href="#viva-questions" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Follow-Up Viva Questions</a>
        <a href="#chat-feedback-box" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Ready-to-Post Chat Reply &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Assignment Prompt Card -->
    <section id="assignment-brief" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue, #2563eb);">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem;">ASSIGNED TASK BRIEF</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-top: 0.2rem;">
            Day 1: Layered Architecture (Controller &rarr; Service &rarr; Repository) &amp; Serverless Entry
          </h2>
        </div>
        <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem;">Assigned to: Bro Phyo Min Htet &amp; Sis Yamin Aye</span>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <strong>Focus:</strong> Understand how incoming HTTP requests are routed and how responsibilities are separated across the three core backend layers in Java 17. Provide a report on each point and post the detailed report for each point in the chat group.
      </p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 0.85rem;">
        <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.85rem;">
          <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
            1. Serverless Function / API Entry &amp; Controller Layer
          </strong>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 1.1rem; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; line-height: 1.45;">
            <li>Explore backend project structure (<code class="code-pill">pom.xml</code>, Java 17 features such as <code class="code-pill">record</code>, <code class="code-pill">sealed</code> classes, or <code class="code-pill">Optional</code>).</li>
            <li>Trace how serverless handlers (<code class="code-pill">@FunctionName</code>, <code class="code-pill">@HttpTrigger</code>) or REST controllers expose endpoints for <code class="code-pill">iBanking_portal</code> and <code class="code-pill">adminconsole</code>.</li>
            <li>Inspect how authentication context (Customer ID from JWT vs. Admin Role/Session from <code class="code-pill">btoken</code>) is extracted in Controller or security middleware.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.85rem;">
          <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
            2. Service &amp; Repository Layers + Hands-On Task
          </strong>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 1.1rem; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; line-height: 1.45;">
            <li><strong>Service Layer:</strong> Identify where business rules live (fee calculation, daily limit verification, account/OTP checks) and how <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code> boundaries work.</li>
            <li><strong>Repository Layer:</strong> Inspect how backend communicates with MSSQL / PostgreSQL (<code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code>, JDBC, native queries).</li>
            <li><strong>Hands-On Task:</strong> Pick 1 customer endpoint and 1 admin endpoint, draw their class dependency chain (<code class="code-pill">Controller &rarr; Service &rarr; Repository</code>), and verify why business logic must never sit inside a Controller or Repository.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Interactive Reviewer Checklist -->
    <section id="reviewer-checklist" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-warning" style="font-size: 0.65rem;">REVIEWER VERIFICATION GATE</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-top: 0.2rem;">
            Master Mentor Review Checklist (Click to Tick)
          </h2>
          <p style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0.15rem 0 0 0;">
            Use this ground-truth checklist when reviewing intern reports and chat group posts. Progress auto-saves in your browser.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;" class="no-print">
          <span class="badge badge-success" id="w5d1-checklist-progress">0 / 12 Checked</span>
          <button id="w5d1-reset-checks" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(460px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
        <!-- Group A: Submission & Layer 1 -->
        <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 1rem;">
          <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em;">
            Part 1: Submission Gate, Java 17 &amp; Controller Layer
          </div>

          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem;">
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c1" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Chat Group Detail Post:</strong> Intern posted each point in detail in the chat group, not just a summary file.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c2" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Maven <code class="code-pill">pom.xml</code> Inspected:</strong> Verified <code class="code-pill">&lt;java.version&gt;17&lt;/java.version&gt;</code>, <code class="code-pill">azure-functions-maven-plugin</code>, <code class="code-pill">mssql-jdbc</code>, <code class="code-pill">postgresql</code>, <code class="code-pill">sequelize</code>, and <code class="code-pill">httputils</code>.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c3" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Java 17 Features Verified:</strong> Identified real <code class="code-pill">Optional&lt;T&gt;</code> usage in request bodies &amp; DAOs vs. Lombok DTOs where Java 17 <code class="code-pill">record</code> / <code class="code-pill">sealed</code> classes could apply.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c4" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Serverless Routing Accuracy:</strong> Contrasted Spring <code class="code-pill">@RestController</code> with Azure <code class="code-pill">@FunctionName</code> + <code class="code-pill">@HttpTrigger</code> and matched the exact HTTP method &amp; route to the Java class.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c5" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Both Portals Represented:</strong> Selected 1 genuine endpoint from <code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> (<code class="code-pill">com.mit.function.*</code>) and 1 genuine endpoint from <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code> (<code class="code-pill">com.function.*</code>).</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c6" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Auth Context Extraction:</strong> Traced <code class="code-pill">SecurityMiddleware.checkAuth()</code> vs. inline <code class="code-pill">TokenUtil.isTokenExpired()</code> + <code class="code-pill">ServerUtil.isBTokenAuth()</code> &rarr; <code class="code-pill">TokenData</code>.</span>
            </label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Group B: Layer 2, Layer 3 & Hands-on -->
        <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 1rem;">
          <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em;">
            Part 2: Service, Repository &amp; Hands-On Architecture Defense
          </div>

          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem;">
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c7" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Service Layer Business Rules:</strong> Identified where OTP verification (<code class="code-pill">OtpService</code>), user/account checks, fee calculation, or limit rules reside.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c8" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong><code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code> &amp; Connection Lifecycle:</strong> Explained atomic commit/rollback purpose of <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code> and noted manual <code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code> connection handling in serverless functions.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c9" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Repository / DAO Layer:</strong> Distinguished between <code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code> ORM methods (<code class="code-pill">findOneSync</code>, <code class="code-pill">createSync</code>) and legacy JDBC <code class="code-pill">PreparedStatement</code> (<code class="code-pill">PayeeDao</code>).</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c10" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Dependency Chain Diagram:</strong> Accurately mapped <code class="code-pill">Controller &rarr; Service &rarr; DAO</code> for both chosen endpoints.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c11" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Why No Business Logic in Controller/Repo:</strong> Defended separation using Reusability, Transaction Integrity, Unit Testability (Mockito), and SQL Decoupling.</span>
            </label>
            <label class="w5-check-row" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
              <input type="checkbox" class="w5d1-check" data-id="c12" style="margin-top: 0.2rem;" />
              <span><strong>Spotted Codebase Anti-Patterns (Bonus):</strong> Identified direct Controller-to-DAO calls (<code class="code-pill">new PayeeDao()</code>) or raw SQL/HTTP calls leaking into Controller/Service classes.</span>
            </label>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Side-by-Side Comparison Matrix -->
    <section id="comparison-matrix" class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <div>
          <span class="badge badge-neutral" style="font-size: 0.65rem;">CODEBASE-VERIFIED SCORECARD</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.1875rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-top: 0.2rem;">
            Intern Submission Audit Matrix (2.11.2026)
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
          <span class="badge badge-success">Mg Phyo Min Htet: 92 / 100 (Approved)</span>
          <span class="badge badge-warning">Ma Yamin Aye: 62 / 100 (Needs Revision)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.8125rem; text-align: left;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-subtle); color: var(--text-primary);">
              <th style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; width: 24%;">Checklist Dimension</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; width: 22%;">Mg Phyo Min Htet</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; width: 22%;">Ma Yamin Aye</th>
              <th style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; width: 32%;">Codebase Ground-Truth Verification</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;">1. <code class="code-pill">pom.xml</code> &amp; Java 17 Features</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Pass (15/15)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-warning">Copied Text (10/15)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Yamin’s Section 1 is word-for-word identical to Phyo’s. Both note <code class="code-pill">Optional</code> is used while <code class="code-pill">record</code> / <code class="code-pill">sealed</code> are not used in legacy DTOs.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;">2. Serverless Route Mapping</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;">
                <span class="badge badge-success">Pass (15/15)</span>
                <div style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: 0.2rem;">
                  <code class="code-pill">POST /api/requestpayeesetup</code><br/>
                  <code class="code-pill">POST /api/addpayee</code><br/>
                  <code class="code-pill">GET /api/changepassword</code>
                </div>
              </td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;">
                <span class="badge badge-rose">Route Mix-Up (6/15)</span>
                <div style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: 0.2rem;">
                  Wrote <code class="code-pill">SaveUserStatus (POST /api/addpayee)</code> &amp; <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus (GET /api/changepassword)</code>
                </div>
              </td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                <strong>Copy-Paste Bug:</strong> Yamin replaced Phyo’s class names with <code class="code-pill">SaveUserStatus</code> and <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus</code> but left Phyo’s URLs (<code class="code-pill">/api/addpayee</code> and <code class="code-pill">/api/changepassword</code>)! Actual routes are <code class="code-pill">POST /api/saveuserstatus</code> and <code class="code-pill">POST /api/UpdateTransactionStatus</code>.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;">3. Dual-Portal Selection (<code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> vs <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code>)</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Pass (10/10)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-rose">Both in ibanking17 (4/10)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus.java</code> is inside <code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> (<code class="code-pill">com.mit.function</code>), <strong>not</strong> <code class="code-pill">admin_console</code>! It is a CAS webhook in <code class="code-pill">ibanking17</code> that calls out to Admin Console.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;">4. Authentication Context Extraction</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Pass (10/10)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-warning">Inaccurate (6/10)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                <code class="code-pill">AddPayee.java</code> uses <code class="code-pill">SecurityMiddleware.checkAuth()</code>. Neither of Yamin’s chosen endpoints uses <code class="code-pill">SecurityMiddleware</code> (and <code class="code-pill">UpdateTransactionStatus</code> has <strong>zero auth validation</strong>).
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;">5. Service Layer &amp; <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Pass (13/15)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-warning">No @Transactional (9/15)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Phyo explicitly addressed <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code> and noted its absence in the serverless implementation. Yamin traced <code class="code-pill">UserService</code> status rules well but omitted <code class="code-pill">@Transactional</code>.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); background: var(--bg-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;">6. Repository Layer (<code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code> &amp; JDBC)</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Outstanding (15/15)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Pass (13/15)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Phyo spotted that <code class="code-pill">com.mit.dao.PayeeDao</code> uses raw JDBC <code class="code-pill">PreparedStatement</code> while <code class="code-pill">UserDao</code>/<code class="code-pill">UserHistoryDao</code> use <code class="code-pill">Sequelize</code> (<code class="code-pill">findOneSync</code>, <code class="code-pill">createSync</code>).
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;">7. Hands-On Chain &amp; Layer Separation Defense</td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-success">Pass (14/20)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;"><span class="badge badge-rose">Missing Defense (14/20)</span></td>
              <td style="padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Phyo spotted direct <code class="code-pill">Controller &rarr; PayeeDao</code> anti-patterns and defended why business logic belongs in <code class="code-pill">Service</code>. Yamin drew the chains but never answered <em>why</em> business logic must not sit in Controller/Repo.
              </td>
            </tr>
